ellie_sales: Heads up — EuroVault (EU-based bank) wants a short POC: SSE streaming, in-stream function/tool calls that trigger downstream webhooks, and strict structured JSON output validated against a schema. They also requested: EU residency, SOC2 evidence, on-prem or VPC option, and committed pricing for 3 months with burst capacity. Can we confirm feasibility and what we'll hand them by EOD?

 tom_presales: Quick clarifying q's: 1) Do they need callbacks (webhook triggered by function) or just function responses in the stream? 2) Is final JSON expected at stream end or as discrete "documents" midstream? 3) Any required fields/schema example?

 ellie_sales: They want webhooks invoked during the stream (low-latency actions), and final envelope per message. Schema minimal: id (string), type (string), evidence (object with keys), items (array of {name, score}). They want us to perform server-side schema validation and reject malformed payloads.

 tom_presales: We can do that. Approach: use SSE with a functions list; when the model emits a function_call event we forward to their webhook. For schema validation we support two modes: (A) stream emits partial JSON chunks and we reconstruct + validate at the end, (B) force model to emit a single JSON document as the final event. Recommend B for reliability. Example Node pattern:

 ```js
 const stream = await client.stream.start({ model: 'redwood-gen-4', stream: 'sse', functions: [fnDef] });
 for await (const ev of stream) {
   if (ev.type === 'function_call') await forwardToWebhook(ev.payload);
   if (ev.type === 'final_json') {
     const ok = validateSchema(ev.json);
     sendAck(ok);
   }
 }
 ```

 chris_infra: Operational notes: for EU residency we can place the POC in eu-west-1 region on Dedicated. For no-cache semantics set route config `cache: false`. For on-prem we can discuss Redwood Private; that'll need an infra discovery call. Dedicated trial: we can provision a 2-week reserved slice (committed) with burst enabled; ops will need an expected QPS and model sequence length.

 nina_security: SOC2 + compliance: we can provide SOC2 Type II summary, DPIA template, and subprocessors list. For on-prem, many controls shift to customer. We need the filled vendor security matrix to pre-answer network/VPN/firewall questions. Also confirm retention: what's their required retention window?

 ellie_sales: They requested 60-day retention, EU-only processing. Also asked about KV/prefix cache — they want to ensure no PII persists.

 chris_infra: Confirmed: we can disable KV/prefix caching for the POC and Dedicated nodes are single-tenant. For Private, storage behavior depends on customer config; we'll note that.

 sara_cs: Proposed presales playbook: 1) ship tiny sample repo (Node + curl samples), 2) provide a sandbox token (14 days), 3) send SOC2 + DPA, 4) offer 2-week Dedicated trial. Who will own the sample code?

 tom_presales: I'll build a minimal repo showing SSE + in-stream function invocation + server-side JSON schema validation using ajv. Will include schema.json and a tiny express webhook handler to demo real-time invocation. Plan to push to git.internal/presales/eurovault-poc by EOD.

 infra-bot: infra: sandbox token created (proj:eurovault-poc-sandbox) expires in 14d. Dedicated trial request queued (ops ticket #EUV-409).

 nina_security: Action items: ellie get vendor matrix completed; I will pre-fill answers and mark items for legal. Include requested DPA clause about EU-only processing.

 ellie_sales: I'll request the matrix now and confirm demo timing. Let's aim for a 30m technical runthrough tomorrow 11:00 CET. Thanks all. :rocket:
